 const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('/workspace/report.md')\np.write_text('''# Staged experiment diagnosis\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Unhealthy.** The frozen held-out evidence is decisive: `eval/nq_test` rises from 0.033 at step 0 to only 0.1673 at step 199 (maximum 0.1683), while effective response length collapses from 932.8 to 12.2 tokens. Held-out truncation falls from 0.3637 to 0.00067, and rollout runtime falls from 28.8 seconds to about 2 seconds. This is short-output degeneration rather than healthy search behavior. The increasing training `raw_reward` (roughly 0.035 early and as high as 0.36 later) is not sufficient evidence of health: normalized rollout rewards and advantages are approximately zero, and the logs show many zero-variance groups.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe custom rollout had three defects that connect directly to the observed behavior:\n\n1. `_passages2string` split each retrieved document into `title` and `text`, then emitted only the title. The policy therefore received little or no retrieved evidence, undermining the search task.\n2. Retrieval observations were appended with `trainable=False`, but the custom function separately built `loss_mask` with ones for every token before overwriting `sample.loss_mask`. Environment context was consequently included in the policy loss. The repaired path gives observation tokens zero loss weight. This is consistent with the abrupt response-length/runtime collapse and near-zero normalized learning signal.\n3. `qa_em_format.compute_score_em` uses `structure_format_score`, `final_format_score`, and `retrieval_score` for shaping; the old reward call supplied only the scorer's unused legacy `format_score`. Valid non-exact trajectories therefore received no intended partial credit. The repaired call supplies 0.2 structure credit and 0.1 each for final-format and retrieval credit.\n\nThe evidence is corroborated by the staged W&B output: early rollouts have response lengths around 1038, truncation 0.3828, and runtime 28.83 seconds; late rollouts have lengths around 9, truncation 0, and runtime 1.97 seconds, while `eval/nq_test` remains near 0.15–0.17.\n\n## Changes\n\n- [generate_with_search.py](/workspace/examples/search-r1/generate_with_search.py:44): include retrieved passage bodies; keep retrieval observations non-trainable in the local loss mask; pass the scorer's actual partial-credit arguments.\n- [run_qwen2.5_3B.sh](/workspace/examples/search-r1/run_qwen2.5_3B.sh:38): pin the run to `/workspace` checkpoints, datasets, corpus, and local retrieval; use 100 rollouts, the required eval dataset slice/interval/sample count and custom paths; route the foreground log to `$AUTORLBENCH_RESULTS/experiment_logs/train.log` and W&B to its `wandb` subdirectory; make offline W&B key handling safe; propagate offline-only environment settings through Ray.\n\nThe read-only scorer, retriever directory, and staged parquet datasets were not modified.\n\n## Expected effect\n\n`eval/nq_test` should improve above the frozen ~0.167 plateau. Rollout raw rewards should become better shaped, with fewer zero-variance groups and nontrivial normalized advantages. Generated search trajectories should retain useful reasoning/evidence instead of converging to 9–12-token responses; the logged effective response length should reflect policy tokens and truncation should remain meaningful rather than collapsing immediately.\n''')\nPY\nwc -c /workspace/report.md; sed -n '1,240p' /workspace/report.md",workdir:"/workspace",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:20000});
