4627:{"timestamp":"2026-11-08T21:41:30.618Z","ordinal":4626,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1bd1b-fd7a-7c13-8048-68e8c300f591","call_id":"call_505ee6436ee7435aae1560143c8cb62c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# Staged experiment diagnosis\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Unhealthy.** The frozen held-out evidence is decisive: `eval/nq_test` rises from 0.033 at step 0 to only 0.1673 at step 199 (maximum 0.1683), while effective response length collapses from 932.8 to 12.2 tokens. Held-out truncation falls from 0.3637 to 0.00067, and rollout runtime falls from 28.8 seconds to about 2 seconds. This is short-output degeneration rather than healthy search behavior. The increasing training `raw_reward` (roughly 0.035 early and as high as 0.36 later) is not sufficient evidence of health: normalized rollout rewards and advantages are approximately zero, and the logs show many zero-variance groups.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe custom rollout had four defects that connect directly to the observed behavior:\n\n1. `_passages2string` split each retrieved document into `title` and `text`, then emitted only the title. The policy therefore received little or no retrieved evidence, undermining the search task.\n2. Retrieval observations were appended with `trainable=False`, but the custom function separately built `loss_mask` with ones for every token before overwriting `sample.loss_mask`. Environment context was consequently included in the policy loss. The repaired path gives observation tokens zero loss weight. This is consistent with the abrupt response-length/runtime collapse and near-zero normalized learning signal.\n3. `qa_em_format.compute_score_em` uses `structure_format_score`, `final_format_score`, and `retrieval_score` for shaping; the old reward call supplied only the scorer's unused legacy `format_score`. Valid non-exact trajectories therefore received no intended partial credit. The repaired call supplies 0.2 structure credit and 0.1 each for final-format and retrieval credit. (The scorer returns 0.3 for a valid retrieval trajectory without an exact answer, and 0.2 for valid formatting without retrieval.)\n4. With log-probability collection enabled, response postprocessing is intentionally skipped to preserve token alignment. Without explicit stop strings, the inference engine could continue emitting text after `</search>` or `</answer>`, adding junk to the trainable trajectory and invalidating otherwise well-formed answers. The repaired generation request stops at both boundaries while retaining the stop token.\n\nThe evidence is corroborated by the staged W&B output: early rollouts have response lengths around 1038, truncation 0.3828, and runtime 28.83 seconds; late rollouts have lengths around 9, truncation 0, and runtime 1.97 seconds, while `eval/nq_test` remains near 0.15–0.17.\n\n## Changes\n\n- [generate_with_search.py](/workspace/examples/search-r1/generate_with_search.py:44): include retrieved passage bodies; require the expected chat-templated string prompt explicitly; stop generation at tool/answer boundaries; keep retrieval observations non-trainable in the local loss mask; pass the scorer's actual partial-credit arguments.\n- [run_qwen2.5_3B.sh](/workspace/examples/search-r1/run_qwen2.5_3B.sh:38): pin the run to `/workspace` checkpoints, datasets, corpus, and local retrieval; use 100 rollouts, the required eval dataset slice/interval/sample count and custom paths; route the foreground log to `$AUTORLBENCH_RESULTS/experiment_logs/train.log` and W&B to its `wandb` subdirectory; make offline W&B key handling safe; propagate offline-only environment settings through Ray; force local offline model/dataset loading.\n- [start_retriver.sh](/workspace/examples/search-r1/start_retriver.sh:8): require the staged `/workspace/e5-base-v2` encoder and fail instead of falling back to a network hub identifier.\n- [report.md](/workspace/report.md): record this diagnosis, evidence, repairs, and expected metric movement.\n\nThe read-only scorer, retriever directory, and staged parquet datasets were not modified.\n\n## Expected effect\n\n`eval/nq_test` should improve above the frozen ~0.167 plateau. Rollout raw rewards should become better shaped, with fewer zero-variance groups and nontrivial normalized advantages. Generated search trajectories should retain useful reasoning/evidence instead of converging to 9–12-token responses; boundary stopping should reduce invalid trailing output; the logged effective response length should reflect policy tokens and truncation should remain meaningful rather than collapsing immediately.\n\n-- changed mtimes --\n2026-11-08 21:41:18.205110000 +0000 4346 report.md\n2026-11-08 20:28:34.041972000 +0000 12754 examples/search-r1/generate_with_search.py\n2026-11-08 21:35:39.244034000 +0000 15383 examples/search-r1/run_qwen2.5_3B.sh\n2026-11-08 19:53:22.964109009 +0000 780 examples/search-r1/start_retriver.sh\n\n-- syntax --\n\n-- protected hashes --\naa0133c8bd6e1b9acf84e6e10a83f7dc9230d693ee495a21005e2eb314a5a261  examples/search-r1/qa_em_format.py\nfef22aa552f8bd50d5cea5cc1f69d8d44fb1dca5c9cda2df737088c52a104ca6  examples/search-r1/local_dense_retriever/download.py\nfdd1f6e5ce177077a50006bf72a26f65d7026325c59df59577f23d24e5cc7d1f  examples/search-r1/local_dense_retriever/retrieval_server.py\nb0ca353be5db159180787ac35f97eb5bce2aa485b2d16382b8a168509b505ade  nq_hotpotqa_train/train.parquet\n5addf24a4b7caee3d320bff4b01c416c708f6afabf810f347c3dea076af1838f  nq_hotpotqa_train/test.parquet\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1bc33-823b-70a2-ad42-f3422e43b435","create_time":1794174090.6182127}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
4669:{"timestamp":"2026-11-08T21:44:58.744Z","ordinal":4668,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0b7fc33f0d7ef410016af0ed58af8487d08a76fb8bf765a589","status":"completed","call_id":"call_41d38c9a441d49a6aeef9209ce7325b6","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"stat -c '%A %a %n' examples/search-r1/run_qwen2.5_3B.sh examples/search-r1/start_retriver.sh examples/search-r1/generate_with_search.py report.md; sed -n '1,120p' examples/search-r1/prepare_data.sh\",workdir:\"/workspace\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:16000}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1bc33-823b-7194-a40c-0a3209d58785","create_time":1794174297.0989537}}}
4670:{"timestamp":"2026-11-08T21:44:58.786Z","ordinal":4669,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1bc33-822d-7342-bc16-3628d4b92e54","turn_id":"01a1bc33-823b-70a2-ad42-f3422e43b435","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fcb690b0-4982-409d-aabf-4373654ee06b","process_id":"71214","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","stat -c '%A %a %n' examples/search-r1/run_qwen2.5_3B.sh examples/search-r1/start_retriver.sh examples/search-r1/generate_with_search.py report.md; sed -n '1,120p' examples/search-r1/prepare_data.sh"],"cwd":"file:///workspace","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"stat -c '%A %a %n' examples/search-r1/run_qwen2.5_3B.sh examples/search-r1/start_retriver.sh examples/search-r1/generate_with_search.py report.md; sed -n '1,120p' examples/search-r1/prepare_data.sh"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"-rw-r--r-- 644 examples/search-r1/run_qwen2.5_3B.sh\n-rw-r--r-- 644 examples/search-r1/start_retriver.sh\n-rw-r--r-- 644 examples/search-r1/generate_with_search.py\n-rw-r--r-- 644 report.md\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Prepare the inputs for the Search-R1 slime recipe:\n#   1. the QA dataset  -> nq_hotpotqa_train/{train,test}.parquet\n#   2. the retrieval corpus -> wiki-18 e5 FAISS index + wiki-18.jsonl\n#\n# It drives the data-preparation subset of the Search-R1 repo that ships next to\n# this recipe (workspace/Search-R1). Nothing here trains a model.\n#\n# Usage:\n#   bash prepare_data.sh                 # dataset + corpus\n#   DATASET_ONLY=1 bash prepare_data.sh  # skip the ~130GB corpus download\n#   CORPUS_ONLY=1  bash prepare_data.sh  # only the retrieval corpus\n#\n# Override any path via the environment variables below.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n# --- locations -------------------------------------------------------------\n# Directory of this script (examples/search-r1), resolved so it works from any cwd.\nHERE=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\n\n# The trimmed Search-R1 repo. Defaults to the copy staged in this workspace\n# (workspace/Search-R1); at container runtime the recipe reads /root/Search-R1,\n# so allow an override.\nSEARCH_R1_DIR=\"${SEARCH_R1_DIR:-$(cd \"$HERE/../../Search-R1\" && pwd)}\"\n\n# Where prepared assets land. Keep them inside the repo's data/ dir so the paths\n# match the recipe's --prompt-data (…/Search-R1/data/nq_hotpotqa_train/…).\nDATA_DIR=\"${DATA_DIR:-$PWD}\"\nDATASET_DIR=\"${DATASET_DIR:-$DATA_DIR/nq_hotpotqa_train}\"\nCORPUS_DIR=\"${CORPUS_DIR:-$DATA_DIR/wiki-18}\"\n\n# Which QA sources to merge. Train mixes NQ+HotpotQA (the recipe default); the\n# test merge can span more sets for evaluation.\nTRAIN_SOURCES=\"${TRAIN_SOURCES:-nq,hotpotqa}\"\nTEST_SOURCES=\"${TEST_SOURCES:-nq,hotpotqa}\"\n\nDATASET_ONLY=\"${DATASET_ONLY:-0}\"\nCORPUS_ONLY=\"${CORPUS_ONLY:-0}\"\n# Re-download even if the target files already exist.\nFORCE=\"${FORCE:-0}\"\n\nif [[ ! -d \"$SEARCH_R1_DIR/scripts/data_process\" ]]; then\n  echo \"error: Search-R1 data-prep scripts not found under: $SEARCH_R1_DIR\" >&2\n  echo \"       set SEARCH_R1_DIR to the trimmed Search-R1 repo.\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\n# The merge scripts import verl.utils.hdfs_io from the repo root.\nexport PYTHONPATH=\"$SEARCH_R1_DIR${PYTHONPATH:+:$PYTHONPATH}\"\n\n# --- 1) QA dataset ---------------------------------------------------------\nprepare_dataset() {\n  local train_parquet=\"$DATASET_DIR/train.parquet\"\n  local test_parquet=\"$DATASET_DIR/test.parquet\"\n\n  if [[ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" && -f \"$train_parquet\" && -f \"$test_parquet\" ]]; then\n    echo \"==> QA parquet already present, skipping ($DATASET_DIR)\"\n    echo \"    -> $train_parquet\"\n    echo \"    -> $test_parquet\"\n    return\n  fi\n\n  echo \"==> Building QA parquet into $DATASET_DIR\"\n  echo \"    train sources: $TRAIN_SOURCES\"\n  echo \"    test  sources: $TEST_SOURCES\"\n  mkdir -p \"$DATASET_DIR\"\n\n  if [[ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" && -f \"$train_parquet\" ]]; then\n    echo \"    train.parquet exists, skipping train merge\"\n  else\n    python \"$SEARCH_R1_DIR/scripts/data_process/qa_search_train_merge.py\" \\\n      --local_dir \"$DATASET_DIR\" --data_sources \"$TRAIN_SOURCES\"\n  fi\n\n  if [[ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" && -f \"$test_parquet\" ]]; then\n    echo \"    test.parquet exists, skipping test merge\"\n  else\n    python \"$SEARCH_R1_DIR/scripts/data_process/qa_search_test_merge.py\" \\\n      --local_dir \"$DATASET_DIR\" --data_sources \"$TEST_SOURCES\"\n  fi\n\n  echo \"    -> $train_parquet\"\n  echo \"    -> $test_parquet\"\n}\n\n# --- 2) retrieval corpus (wiki-18 e5) --------------------------------------\nprepare_corpus() {\n  local index=\"$CORPUS_DIR/e5_Flat.index\"\n  local jsonl=\"$CORPUS_DIR/wiki-18.jsonl\"\n\n  if [[ \"$FORCE\" != \"1\" && -f \"$index\" && -f \"$jsonl\" ]]; then\n    echo \"==> wiki-18 corpus already present, skipping ($CORPUS_DIR)\"\n    echo \"    -> $index\"\n    echo \"    -> $jsonl\"\n    return\n  fi\n\n  echo \"==> Downloading wiki-18 e5 index + corpus into $CORPUS_DIR\"\n  echo \"    NOTE: the assembled index is ~130GB; ensure disk + bandwidth.\"\n  mkdir -p \"$CORPUS_DIR\"\n\n  # Pulls PeterJinGo/wiki-18-e5-index (part_aa, part_ab) and\n  # PeterJinGo/wiki-18-corpus (wiki-18.jsonl.gz) from the HuggingFace Hub.\n  python \"$SEARCH_R1_DIR/scripts/download.py\" --save_path \"$CORPUS_DIR\"\n\n  echo \"    Assembling e5_Flat.index from shards\"\n  cat \"$CORPUS_DIR\"/part_* > \"$index\"\n  rm -f \"$CORPUS_DIR\"/part_*\n\n  if [[ -f \"$CORPUS_DIR/wiki-18.jsonl.gz\" ]]; then\n    echo \"    Decompressing wiki-18.jsonl\"\n    gzip -df \"$CORPUS_DIR/wiki-18.jsonl.gz\"\n  fi\n\n  echo \"    -> $index\"\n  echo \"    -> $jsonl\"\n}\n\n# --- run -------------------------------------------------------------------\nif [[ \"$CORPUS_ONLY\" == \"1\" ]]; then\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5658}},"started_at_ms":1794174298786,"completed_at_ms":1794174298786}}
